WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.959
Hello again friends. You're about to do
lesson five in the course. So let's

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:05.939
just jump right.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.340
In and our last lesson, we looked at organizing your thoughts clearly.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:18.660
In lesson 5, we'll look at effective
pauses. Concise tip number five is pause

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.490
to add emphasis. And this really is a
conciseness tip, however, it's going to

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:28.230
make you sound much more clear and
certainly much more confident. Pauses in

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.130
the wrong places can make you sound
long-winded. Pauses in the right place

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:37.260
make you sound clear and concise. And good pauses emphasize your points and add a

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.780
confident cadence. It gives your speech a
rhythm or a tempo that those

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.149
professional speakers and those leaders
have. Pauses are really like a secret

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:52.739
weapon in communication. Ralph Richardson, a well-known actor on the stage and

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:57.960
screen from years ago said, "The most
precious things in speech are pauses."

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.670
And I could not agree more.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.049
Strategy number one. Pause at the end of
sentences.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:07.530
That's where your pauses belong. It makes you sound more confident. It lets

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.189
listeners accept and remember your
message. During that pause they get to

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:15.240
process it for just a moment and it
gives you a natural stopping place to

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.310
end you're talking turn.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.550
That's one of the goals of being a
concise, clear, and confident communicator.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.799
Is you make your point, and as we said in
an earlier lesson, then you zip it. And it

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.810
allows you to have a back-and-forth or a
dialogue with other people because the

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.880
pause gives them a place to jump in.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.369
So let's listen to where the pauses are
here. We have a few items to cover today.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:43.409
We'll look at our social media campaign. We'll look at our overall growth. And

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:47.610
Erin will take suggestions about
changes to the website. Now these pauses

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.470
are in the right place. They're where the
punctuation is at the end of the nice

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.780
concise sentences.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.430
These are good examples of concise
sentences. From an earlier lesson. And if

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.659
we were to visualize this, it looks a
little bit more like bullets in a list

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.860
where the pause comes right at the end
of that bulleted item and then you go on

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.330
to the next item.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.870
These are like headlines that we talked
about in an earlier lesson.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.099
Or, even they're not funny, but the length
of a punchline for a joke and that's

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:23.159
where the pauses belong. Pauses at the end literally punctuate your statements for

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:27.540
listeners. It helps them separate the
ideas because you have with the sound of

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.720
your voice separated your ideas.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.500
You should only pause for about one
second, just long enough to say the word

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.299
pause in your head.

00:02:36.299 --> 00:02:40.590
Sometimes people pause for two or three
or more sentences [seconds] to add that dramatic feel,

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.790
I don't think that's necessary in most
cases. Just long enough to say the word

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.670
"pause" or "period" in your head.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.920
Strategy number two. Avoid mid-thought
pauses. Pauses in the middle of your

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.629
statements really make it drag. And it'll
sound labored and long-winded even if

00:02:57.629 --> 00:03:02.700
you're not using a lot of words. So let's
listen to what it sounds like when the pauses

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.709
are in the wrong place.

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:10.799
We have a few items to cover today we'll
look at our social media campaign we'll

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:16.590
look at our overall growth and Erin
will take suggestions about changes to

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:23.069
the website. So it doesn't sound right. It
sounds like we're hanging, we're waiting

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:27.900
for that next moment that just, oh
finish your thought, and you may have

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.290
listened to people in conversation with
a pause in the middle. And it can take an

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.849
ordinary sentence and make it really
sound extra-long. So we want to pause in

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:41.970
the right places. Strategy 3 is to pause
to separate key ideas. When you were, for

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.389
example, giving a roadmap to set up a
meeting or presentation, we want to pause

00:03:45.389 --> 00:03:50.310
between items. In that meeting or
presentation and anytime your listing

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.500
items--two or three or four items--you
want to pause where the commas are. So

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.540
here's a sentence. Eighties rock is the
best because it has loud drums, crunchy

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:06.510
guitars, and soaring locals. So we're
pausing where we see the punctuation

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:11.940
would naturally be. And it gives it that
nice confident sound where the ideas are

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.769
separated. Some people, by the way would say screeching locals instead of soaring

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:21.089
vocals but I was trying to be kind
because I'm a big fan of eighties rock.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:26.250
So pause in the right place for clarity
and emphasis. Our take-away strategies are

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.900
to pause at the end of sentences. Avoid
mid-thought pauses that give it that

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.669
dragging sound. And to pause to separate
ideas in a list, especially things

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:40.709
like a preview statements in a
presentation or when you're setting up a meeting.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.300
Your task is to practice pausing in all
your communication to have that clarity

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.979
in the next few days. It's also going to
sound, makes it sound much more confident,

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:55.260
much more concise for your listeners. Up
next we are going to work on avoiding

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.080
fillers and I look forward to seeing you
in that lesson.

